  by: agent  # 338a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 338a
  clock: 2  # 338a
  nonce: 338a  # 338a
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. REPRODUCES,\nunchanged, on this item's own filed pair:\n\n    http.Get(u)   [package-qualified FREE FUNCTION] -> cc=method\n    c.Get(u)      [value-receiver METHOD]           -> cc=method\n    os.Getwd()    [package-qualified free function] -> cc=method\n    f.Close()     [method on typed local]           -> cc=method\n\ngo.py does now emit call_construct='function' at three sites (~2998, ~3044,\n~3105), but none of them fires for a call into an UNRESOLVED external package\n-- which is the population the io-boundary F3 gate reads. The field is still\nconstant across the construct distinction it exists to record.\n\nPhase 6 (recall), owner-gated. Status unchanged: violated."  # 338a
- op: discuss  # 320f
  at: '2026-08-27T15:58:23Z'  # 320f
  by: agent  # 320f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 320f
  clock: 3  # 320f
  nonce: 320f  # 320f
  message: "CORPUS-WIDE EVIDENCE for this item, from the 2026-08-27 fundamental concept\naudit of call_construct (write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-call_construct_08272026.md).\n\nThis item's statement -- \"the field records the SYNTAX, not the construct its\nname promises\" -- is now measured beyond Go, on 42 cached surveys\n(lutuh_scope_08242026), 261,365 stamped edges, 19 languages.\n\n1. call_construct is NOT derivable from the callee's Symbol.kind: over\n   261,277 resolved call edges they disagree 85.8% of the time. The single\n   largest honest-disagreement cell is function -> method at 19,611 edges\n   (the converse of this item's Go case), plus method -> function at 471.\n   So the confusion is bidirectional and not Go-specific.\n\n2. In the population where it actually costs something -- external callees\n   whose (module, name) matches an io_primitives row, so the catalogue's own\n   declared kind is available as ground truth -- call_construct disagrees\n   with that declared kind 71.8% of the time (3,355 of 4,672). The\n   method -> function cell there is 867 edges, which is this item's defect\n   measured against the catalogue rather than against a fixture.\n\n3. Scope note: the 2,434 remote -> function and 54 application -> function\n   cells in the same measurement are a DIFFERENT defect (erlang/haskell\n   stamping locality and synonym words on a construct key) and are filed\n   separately as WI-kohig. They are not part of this item.\n\nNO STATUS CHANGE PROPOSED. The item reproduces; this is evidence for sizing,\nnot a closure. The audit also filed INV-pimir for the consumer-side join that\nmakes this field's inaccuracy actionable, and that item cites this one as\nrelated-not-duplicate."  # 320f
